<!--
    Cloud-IDE hub — first Spanish locale. The hub is an original APK (not one
    of the three vendored forks it switches between), it ships from
    ship-cloud-ide.yml, and until this file it had no translated locale at
    all: every one of its 52 strings rendered in English on a phone set to
    Spanish. Nobody had reported it.

    LEFT IN ENGLISH ON PURPOSE, because a Spanish systems engineer says them in
    English and a translation would read as a different concept: backend, host,
    SSH, GHCR, IPC, tag, fork, endpoint, sshd, Termux, Nix-on-Droid. Shell
    commands and paths inside cfg_terminal_setup_steps are literal input and
    are byte-for-byte identical to the English — translating `pkg install
    openssh` would be a broken instruction, not a translated one.
-->
